  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is for RNA-only multiprofile scvi_n200, with avgpool at 0.650 accuracy and transformer only marginally higher at 0.653, while image-only resnet50 multiprofile avgpool is much weaker at 0.328. The key uncertainty is whether simple multimodal fusion adds value beyond the strong RNA baseline. config_030 keeps the promising RNA encoder/profile setting and the already-tested image encoder/aggregation, adding only concat fusion, so it directly compares multimodal performance against RNA-only config_005 and image-only config_011. This is the best next experiment because it isolates the effect of fusion/modality before introducing new image encoders or more complex aggregation/fusion choices."
